{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -8 /tmp/8f3-deletion.log; rg -n 'yin.vm.(semantic|linearize|code)(\\\\s|\\\\]|/)' src test --glob '\"'!*.md'\"'; git diff --check; git diff --stat | tail -6; sed -n '610,627p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; head -13 src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize.cljc; sed -n '65,73p' src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Running tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting dao.space.query-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.rule-r-test\n test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc                    |   13 +-\n test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc                        |   20 +-\n test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc                   |   11 +-\n test/yin/vm/ucf_test.cljc                          |  738 --------------\n test/yin/vm_test.cljc                              |    2 +-\n 56 files changed, 369 insertions(+), 5518 deletions(-)\n   `:exporting` or `:ended`, read from `:yin.k/gate`.\"\n  [state]\n  (:yin.k/gate state))\n\n\n;; Bytecode Opcodes\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Shared instruction set for stack and register bytecode VMs.\n\n\n(def schema\n  \"DaoDB schema for :yin/ AST datoms.\n   Complete data model for the Universal AST as queryable datoms.\"\n  {;; Ref attributes (entity references, tempid resolution)\n   :yin/body {:db/valueType :db.type/ref},\n   :yin/operator {:db/valueType :db.type/ref},\n   :yin/operands {:db/valueType :db.type/ref,\n                  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many},\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize\n  \"`project`: the Universal AST → the register-shaped canonical vector\n   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.3).\n\n   One flattening, two lanes: the datom\n   lane reads `:yin/*` datoms through an entity index, the row lane reads\n   code-as-tuples rows (§5.1) by the grammar table's positions. Both hand\n   the same walk a node reader, so the order is shared by construction:\n   operator, then operands left to right; a conditional's test,\n   consequent, alternate; occurrences expanded positionally; saturated\n   defaults; lambda bodies out of line after the main sequence, in one\n   FIFO queue that bodies discovered inside bodies join at the back.\n\n;;\n;; A semantic VM between instructions is a code segment plus register window —\n;; {:segment :pc :value :window :env :k} — all plain data (yin.vm.semantic.md\n;; §7). Nothing travels off-stream: the handoff batch is the AST's\n;; `:yin/*` datoms followed by one registers datom whose value is EDN\n;; text, so the receiver rebuilds the machine from bytes it read, not from a\n;; host object it shares with the sender. Definitions the program made\n;; (symbol-keyed store entries) travel with the registers; primitives,\n;; modules, and the FFI pair are the receiving composition's.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
