leted-GMT: {now:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S} GMT',f'Completed-Local: {now.astimezone(datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(hours=7))):%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S} +07','Coding-Agent: codex','Session-ID: unavailable (not exposed by this API session)','', '# 8f-3 engineer report', '', 'Base: srvm-phase8f3 @ c55a6ceb. Uncommitted and unstaged. No rename, docs edits, src/yang edits, or manifest-golden regeneration. Nine permitted C4 files changed; linked_harness was already on the new kernel.', '', '## Implementation and ordering', '', 'The ruling explicitly documents that UCF step 4b cannot compile before deleting its old semantic caller. Consumer ports and their lanes therefore ran first; UCF shrink, old kernel deletion and opcode/opcase deletion were one final compile unit. No compatibility shim or second v4 batch grammar was added.', '', '- Ports use semantic-register/load-ast for AST datoms and load-vector after semantic-register.linearize/project-rows for row media. Existing retained backends still derive images from project.', '- test_utils keeps the walker constructor and ports the encoder composition; source envelopes select and validate their member before project-rows with the source origin.', '- Remote transport context helpers preserve window and deliver; the transport still carries caller-supplied context verbatim.', '- Demo transfer carries AST datoms and EDN register-window state; receiver derives its code through load-ast, using the carried AST stamp.', '- D2 segment relation uses scan/segment-rows over project; join pattern is [\"'$code _ _ :store-put _ ?key & _]. Rule R stamp legs use register loaders.'\"', '- UCF contains code-address only. Old semantic/linearize/code files, four old test files, vm/opcode-table and opcase are deleted. Stale source/test prose naming deleted vars was fixed.', '', '## Counts and verification', '',f'Static deftest extraction uses the same regex and file suffixes on a frozen HEAD scratch copy and the final tree: {sum(map(len,before.values()))} -> {sum(map(len,after.values()))}; {len(removed)} old-file forms removed, {len(added)} carried-over forms added. No surviving-file test was deleted or renamed. Estimates in the brief are each one higher than these four actual file counts: semantic 24, linearize 22, code 12, UCF 23.', '', 'Per-step static counts: consumer ports 4418 -> 4418; initial coverage carryover 4418 -> 4429; kernel deletion 4429 -> 4348; final store/gensym and tail/non-tail carryover 4348 -> 4350. All test commands were foreground and sequential; no Node/Dart lane was launched.', '', '| Lane | Tests | Assertions | Result |', '|---|---:|---:|---|', '| First engine/FFI/poll/continuation port | 29 | 133 | pass |', '| Observer/query/attach/gate/heap/telemetry port | 167 | 1355 | pass |', '| Other VM consumers, retained backends and remote transport | 259 | 3098 | pass |', '| Nine changed C4 namespaces, -e :slow | 118 | 2017 | pass |', '| Rule R and handoff demo | 29 | 291 | pass |', '| Initial carried-over coverage | 44 | 631 | pass |', '| Deletion/UCF compile lane | 197 | 2092 | pass |', '| Final coverage plus continuation/FFI | 50 | 384 | pass |', '| Whole JVM quick tier | PENDING | PENDING | PENDING |', '', 'Kondo command: clj -M:kondo --lint src test. Baseline was git archive HEAD src test extracted to /tmp/8f3-baseline and linted from the same working directory/config. Before and after: 27 errors, 63 warnings; no new diagnostics after normalizing scratch prefix and line/column positions. One informational diagnostic disappeared with linearize_test. Two transient duplicate-require warnings were fixed.', '', 'Truthful intermediate results: the first larger lane could not load Python3Lexer before generation. bb gen:python-antlr failed in the sandbox with UnresolvedAddressException (and sandbox sysctl teardown denial); the approved network-enabled retry generated the parser successfully. Initial port runs exposed old stack/context/model assumptions and envelope selection; fixes retained the assertions and final lane results are above. A final carried-over test had an unmatched delimiter; targeted kondo and a bracket-tracing script found it, it was corrected, kondo rerun and final focused tests passed. Whole JVM quick tier used approved loopback access.', '', 'Logs: /tmp/8f3-{port-lane,port-lane2-final,port-lane3-final,c4,port-lane4,coverage-complete,deletion,final-coverage-retry,quick,kondo-before,kondo-final}.log.', '', '## Every removed deftest', '', 'Paths below are relative to test/yin/vm. Surviving replacements below use the same base unless a full path is shown. A removed v3 fixture is retired only where it specifies the deleted grammar/layout/API; language and VM facts are carried or mapped explicitly.', '', '| Deleted-file deftest | Disposition and surviving fact |', '|---|---|']\nfor f,n in removed:\n if f.endswith('/semantic_test.cljc'):why=sem[n]\n elif f.endswith('/linearize_test.cljc'):why=lin[n]\n elif f.endswith('/ucf_test.cljc'):why='Retired per Architect ruling R2: hand-assembled v3 segment batches, v3 canonicalization or stack safepoint/activation shape. Register frame/safepoint facts live in semantic_register/frame_test, safepoint_harness_test and effects_test; code-address remains covered by register linearize/code/scan tests.'\n elif f.endswith('/code_test.cljc'):\n  if n.startswith('project-segment'):why='V3 projection fixture retired; address/pc/tuple projection survives in semantic_register/scan_test/segment-rows-carry-a-and-pc and dao/space/query_test/code-joins-store-put-key-to-ast-by-value.'\n  else:why='Retired v3 segment/vector grammar, datom entity/pc/operand shapes or stack terminator rules. V4 grammar coverage lives in semantic_register/code_test/every-item-has-a-refusal-row, refusal-rows-name-rule-and-pc and every-golden-is-accepted.'\n else:raise Exception((f,n))\n lines.append(f'| {Path(f).name}/{n} | {why} |')\nlines+=['','## Per-consumer assertion ledger','','Unchanged means the assertions and expectations are unchanged; setup/loaders/images now use the register kernel. Adapted entries identify structural/format inputs or fields that changed. The following includes every deftest in each changed surviving old-kernel consumer (including tests independent of the kernel), so no consumer test is omitted. No consumer assertion is retired. The 13 added forms listed above are the explicitly carried language tests, described in the deletion ledger.','']\nfor f in ported:\n lines += [f'### {f}', '', '| Deftest | Assertion status |', '|---|---|']\n for n in before[f]:lines.append(f'| {n} | {overrides.get((f,n),\\\"Unchanged; register loader/projection or shared fixture setup ported.\\\")} |')\n lines.append('')\nlines+=['## Scope and remaining gates','','No staged changes; no commits. No docs or src/yang modified. Descriptor/address pins and C4 manifest goldens unchanged. Optional P3 renaming/deduplication was left alone. The semantic-register namespace/file rename is still 8f-2. C4 manifest regeneration is still 8f-4. Node/Dart and phase landing gates remain with the orchestrator.','', 'Open design questions: none identified.','', 'PENDING']\nreport.write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n');Path('/tmp/8f3-report-path').write_text(str(report));print(report)\nPY\npython3 /tmp/8f3-report.py\"","aggregated_output":"collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
