{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '708,730p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc; head -14 src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc; sed -n '177,184p' src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc; rg -n 'yin.vm.code|yin.vm.linearize|semantic.cljc' src test --glob '\"'!*.md'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '708,730p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc; head -14 src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc; sed -n '177,184p' src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc; rg -n 'yin.vm.code|yin.vm.linearize|semantic.cljc' src test --glob '\"'!*.md'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"      :closure\n      (let [arity (nth inst 1), body-pc (nth inst 2)]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :stack (conj stack\n                            (values/closure\n                              (:owner vm)\n                              (cond-> {:type :closure, :arity arity,\n                                       :body-pc body-pc, :frames frames}\n                                store-of (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n      ;; The named VM (semantic.cljc) keeps a separate `val` accumulator\n      ;; distinct from its operand stack `St`, so `:push` there commits\n      ;; `val` onto `St` (St <- St ++ [val]). This machine has no such\n      ;; split: every value-producing case already conjes its result\n      ;; straight onto `:stack`. By the time control reaches a `:push`,\n      ;; the value it would push is already there -- so here it is a no-op\n      ;; that only advances `pc`. Every value-producing opcode below\n      ;; (:stream-*, :gensym, :current-continuation, :resume, and the\n      ;; restore after :ffi-call) honours this, or a `:push` immediately\n      ;; after it would silently drop the value -- there is no `val`\n      ;; register to recover it from.\n      :push\n(ns datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff\n  \"Handoff payload keys for Yin VM v2 continuation transfer.\n\n   v1 handed a continuation between a register VM and a stack VM, so it needed\n   one key list per engine shape. For the ast-walker there is one payload\n   shape and one key list, and the two endpoints differ only in which VM they\n   are. The semantic VM's handoff, below, ships in-band instead.\n\n   What the payload carries: the CESK machine (`:control`, `:env`, `:k`,\n   `:store`), the scheduler (`:ready-queue`, `:wait-set`, `:parked`,\n   `:id-counter`), the observable state (`:halted?`, `:blocked?`, `:value`),\n   and the loaded program (`:program`). What it deliberately omits:\n\n   - `:in-stream` and `:in-cursor`. The v2 VM owns no program medium —\n\n(defn semantic-registers\n  \"The plain-data registers of a shippable semantic VM, stamped with the\n   AST contract its shipped program was admitted under. A primitive the\n   program resolved (a `+` resolved before its call) travels by name; any other\n   host function throws, as does a VM holding stream handles, which would\n   arrive as references to nothing.\"\n  [vm-state]\ntest/dao/space/query_test.cljc:1429:;; yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §4.5/§7.7: whether a :variable row is free or\ntest/dao/space/query_test.cljc:1831:          raises (`{:effect …}` in semantic.cljc's hot loop); FFI, park,\ntest/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc:605:   free at its operand occurrence (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md section 4.5).\"\ntest/yin/vm_test.cljc:297:;; Semantic bytecode (docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2, §7.2)\ntest/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_effects_test.cljc:12:   onto this VM, `yin.vm.linearize` onto the semantic VM, B4's parity\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:32:  \"`((fn [x] (+ x 1)) 10)`, the same worked example `yin.vm.linearize-test`\ntest/yin/vm/ledger_test.cljc:3:   (`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` §5.2, §8).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:4:   or a datom batch (§9.1, `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:995:;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1673:   (`semantic.cljc`). Two directions: `:tags` over every §2.3 syntax tag\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1682:   `yin.vm.linearize`), so it is not re-stated as a map here. Its \\\"other\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:3:   (`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` §5.2, §8).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:719:      ;; The named VM (semantic.cljc) keeps a separate `val` accumulator\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:9:   (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §6.5) and committed as ONE atomic transaction\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
