{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,52p' collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md; tail -8 collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport collections,re\n\ndef diag(file):\n c=collections.Counter()\n for l in Path(file).read_text().splitlines():\n  m=re.match(r'(.+?):\\\\d+:\\\\d+: (.*)',l)\n  if m:c[m[1].replace('/tmp/8f3-baseline/',''),m[2]]+=1\n return c\nprint('Final new diagnostics:',list((diag('/tmp/8f3-kondo-final-tree.log')-diag('/tmp/8f3-kondo-before.log')).items()))\np=Path('collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md');print('Pending markers:',p.read_text().count('PENDING'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-15 08:49:34 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 15:49:34 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: unavailable (not exposed by this API session)\n\n# 8f-3 engineer report\n\nBase: srvm-phase8f3 @ c55a6ceb. Uncommitted and unstaged. No rename, docs edits, src/yang edits, or manifest-golden regeneration. Nine permitted C4 files changed; linked_harness was already on the new kernel.\n\n## Implementation and ordering\n\nThe ruling explicitly documents that UCF step 4b cannot compile before deleting its old semantic caller. Consumer ports and their lanes therefore ran first; UCF shrink, old kernel deletion and opcode/opcase deletion were one final compile unit. No compatibility shim or second v4 batch grammar was added.\n\n- Ports use semantic-register/load-ast for AST datoms and load-vector after semantic-register.linearize/project-rows for row media. Existing retained backends still derive images from project.\n- test_utils keeps the walker constructor and ports the encoder composition; source envelopes select and validate their member before project-rows with the source origin.\n- Remote transport context helpers preserve window and deliver; the transport still carries caller-supplied context verbatim.\n- Demo transfer carries AST datoms and EDN register-window state; receiver derives its code through load-ast, using the carried AST stamp.\n- D2 segment relation uses scan/segment-rows over project; join pattern is [$code _ _ :store-put _ ?key & _]. Rule R stamp legs use register loaders.\n- UCF contains code-address only. Old semantic/linearize/code files, four old test files, vm/opcode-table and opcase are deleted. Stale source/test prose naming deleted vars was fixed.\n\n## Counts and verification\n\nStatic deftest extraction uses the same regex and file suffixes on a frozen HEAD scratch copy and the final tree: 4418 -> 4352; 81 old-file forms removed, 15 carried-over forms added. No surviving-file test was deleted or renamed. Estimates in the brief are each one higher than these four actual file counts: semantic 24, linearize 22, code 12, UCF 23.\n\nPer-step static counts: consumer ports 4418 -> 4418; initial coverage carryover 4418 -> 4429; kernel deletion 4429 -> 4348; final store/gensym and tail/non-tail carryover 4348 -> 4350; final diagnostic/provenance carryover 4350 -> 4352. All test commands were foreground and sequential; no Node/Dart lane was launched.\n\n| Lane | Tests | Assertions | Result |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| First engine/FFI/poll/continuation port | 29 | 133 | pass |\n| Observer/query/attach/gate/heap/telemetry port | 167 | 1355 | pass |\n| Other VM consumers, retained backends and remote transport | 259 | 3098 | pass |\n| Nine changed C4 namespaces, -e :slow | 118 | 2017 | pass |\n| Rule R and handoff demo | 29 | 291 | pass |\n| Initial carried-over coverage | 44 | 631 | pass |\n| Deletion/UCF compile lane | 197 | 2092 | pass |\n| Final coverage plus continuation/FFI | 50 | 384 | pass |\n| Whole JVM quick tier, -e :slow | 4000 | 249194 | pass; two prebuilt Dart-peer probes skipped |\n| Final diagnostic/provenance carryover lane | 48 | 1302 | pass |\n\nKondo command: clj -M:kondo --lint src test. Baseline was git archive HEAD src test extracted to /tmp/8f3-baseline and linted from the same working directory/config. Before and after: 27 errors, 63 warnings; no new diagnostics after normalizing scratch prefix and line/column positions. One informational diagnostic disappeared with linearize_test. Two transient duplicate-require warnings were fixed.\n\nTruthful intermediate results: the first larger lane could not load Python3Lexer before generation. bb gen:python-antlr failed in the sandbox with UnresolvedAddressException (and sandbox sysctl teardown denial); the approved network-enabled retry generated the parser successfully. Initial port runs exposed old stack/context/model assumptions and envelope selection; fixes retained the assertions and final lane results are above. A final carried-over test had an unmatched delimiter; targeted kondo and a bracket-tracing script found it, it was corrected, kondo rerun and final focused tests passed. Whole JVM quick tier used approved loopback access. Its production logic is the final production logic; two additional coverage tests and code-docstring corrections followed that run and were checked by the final focused lane. Skipped probes: a-dart-dialer-reads-a-jvm-server (build/ws-project-peer absent) and a-dart-client-attaches-to-this-jvm-server (build/yin-repl-peer absent). No Dart build was attempted, as directed.\n\nLogs: /tmp/8f3-{port-lane,port-lane2-final,port-lane3-final,c4,port-lane4,coverage-complete,deletion,final-coverage-retry,quick,delivery-coverage,kondo-before,kondo-final,kondo-delivery,kondo-final-tree}.log.\n\n## Every removed deftest\n\nPaths below are relative to test/yin/vm. Surviving replacements below use the same base unless a full path is shown. A removed v3 fixture is retired only where it specifies the deleted grammar/layout/API; language and VM facts are carried or mapped explicitly.\n\n| Deleted-file deftest | Disposition and surviving fact |\n|---|---|\n| linearize_test.cljc/lowered-segments-are-well-formed | V3 batch shape retired. V4 validity: semantic_register/linearize_test/goldens-are-well-formed. |\n\n## Scope and remaining gates\n\nNo staged changes; no commits. No docs or src/yang modified. Descriptor/address pins and C4 manifest goldens unchanged. Optional P3 renaming/deduplication was left alone. The semantic-register namespace/file rename is still 8f-2. C4 manifest regeneration is still 8f-4. Node/Dart and phase landing gates remain with the orchestrator.\n\nOpen design questions: none identified.\n\nREADY\nFinal new diagnostics: [(('test/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc', 'info: Single argument to str already is a string'), 1)]\nPending markers: 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
